# Git (plextraktbox)

This repo uses [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) so
semantic-release can bump on `main`. Local `commit-msg` hook (`.githooks/`) and
PR-title CI both enforce the format.

- Subject: `type: description`, `type(scope): description`, or `type!: description`
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `revert`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`
- No trailing period on the subject
- Optional short body focusing on **why**
- No Jira IDs
- Only commit when explicitly requested; never push unless asked

Examples: `feat: add mobile nav drawer`, `fix: retry Trakt token refresh on 401`,
`chore: tighten API health badge typography`

**Releases (Phase 19):** Commits that land on `main` (direct push or squash-merge PR
title) must be Conventional Commits. CI also checks PR titles via
`.github/workflows/pr-title.yml`.
